{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nTwenty-seven bugs in the fortnight defect review were tests that could not fail or that burned CI time: absent-string subprocess oracles with no return-code check (`0e1d-c698-c38d-4c3e`, `1241-b83c-f8c7-40bf`), a test burning the full 120 s Jira readiness budget per xdist worker (`e394-9433-c839-4c9f`), a timeout oracle expiring after its watchdog fires (`9bb7-4430-1202-4d93`). All closed.\n\nState of the tree:\n\n- `pytest-timeout==2.4.0` is pinned at `pyproject.toml:251`.\n- `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` sets `addopts = \"--strict-markers --strict-config\"` but no `timeout` / `timeout_method` / `timeout_func_only`, so `make test` and bare local `pytest` have no per-test budget. Only 4 `@pytest.mark.timeout` marks exist tree-wide (`test_review_bot.py:1806`; `test_opcert_service_app.py:158,206,268`).\n- The budget lives only on CI command lines: `_build-and-test.yml:658` (default tier) and `:673` (integration tier), both `--timeout=300 --timeout-method=thread`.\n- Ruff 0.16.3 selects `E,F,W,I,UP,B,BLE001,T201,SIM115,ASYNC,DTZ,RUF` with `ignore = [\"RUF001\",\"RUF002\",\"RUF003\"]`; no `PLW1510`, no `PT`. `make lint` runs `ruff check $(sources)`, `sources = src tests scripts` (`Makefile:13`).\n- `scripts/check_wall_clock_asserts.py` and `check_raw_git_writes.py` exist, run in CI only (`_build-and-test.yml:181-198`), are absent from `make lint`, and both exit 0 today.\n\nBacklog (`ruff check --statistics src tests scripts`): **PLW1510 = 336, zero fixes even under `--unsafe-fixes`**; **PT = 1811**, only 37 safely auto-fixable — PT018 1513, PT011 84, PT019 69, PT006 57, PT001 37, PT022 19, PT017 15, PT007 7, PT013 4, PT008 2, PT021 2, PT012 1, PT028 1.\n\nRuntime: `pytest -m unit -n 4 --dist worksteal -q --timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread` ran 11 m 16 s, 5097 passed, **zero** `Failed: Timeout` (the 6 failures + 4 errors were the environmental \"repo HEAD moved\" guard). The `timeout=120..300` values in test sources are subprocess ceilings, not durations: the unit tier already fits inside 20 s. The integration tier is not yet measured.\n\nOperator decision (2026-08-21): adopt only common practice in maintained OSS projects; a 20 s per-test budget with an explicit override for tests that must be slow.\n\n## Approach\n1. **Ruff, per code.** Add the eleven codes in the first AC's selector to `[tool.ruff.lint] select` — 481 findings, cleared here. `PT018`/`PT011`/`PT019` (1666) are deliberately NOT selected; the `select` comment says so in place. PLW1510 is cleared with explicit `check=False` where the call already inspects `returncode`, `check=True` only where an unchecked non-zero exit is a bug.\n2. **Local budget in the ini.** Add the three keys in the fourth AC to `[tool.pytest.ini_options]`.\n3. **Mark the slow integration tests.** Measure that tier at `--timeout=20`, then give each over-budget test `@pytest.mark.timeout(N, func_only=True)` with a one-line comment naming why. No exemption without a comment.\n4. **Lower, do not drop, the CI flags.** `_build-and-test.yml:658` and `:673` go `--timeout=300` -> `20`, keeping `--timeout-method=thread`.\n5. **Drift guard.** One new assertion in `test_ci_workflow_parity.py`: the `--timeout=` on those two steps equals the ini `timeout`.\n6. **`make lint` reachability.** Append both hygiene scripts to the `lint` recipe, as `check_comment_hygiene.py` was by task `2d9a-78c5-5f87-4a22`. No `if [ -f ]` guard: `make lint` runs the patchset's own Makefile.\n\nNot adopted (no maintained tool does it): lints for subprocess `timeout=`, `sleep` budgets, `os.environ.copy()`, `sys.modules` writes, foreign `.git/` writes.\n\n## Constraints\n- **PT codes go in `select`, never `ignore`.** `tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py:73` (`test_ruff_ignore_is_exactly_the_ruf_unicode_deferral`) asserts `[tool.ruff.lint].ignore == [\"RUF001\",\"RUF002\",\"RUF003\"]` exactly, and `test_ruff_lint_has_no_extend_ignore` forbids `extend-ignore`, so selecting a family then silencing most of it fails CI. Per-code selection is the project's own precedent: the `[tool.ruff.lint]` comment records \"We take SIM115 only, not the wider SIM group\".\n- **`--timeout=` must not be removed from any workflow.** `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:718` (`test_every_ci_pytest_lane_has_a_per_test_hang_guard`) sweeps every workflow pytest step and requires both `--timeout=` and `--timeout-method=thread` (`89d5-61da-b621-47f8`, `d835-1846-95d1-4d84`). Dropping them so the ini applies turns that guard red.\n- **Eleven other `--timeout=` lanes stay untouched**, each calibrated for external / live-service / eval suites that run for minutes: `external-integration.yml:245,405,514,625,765`, `_optionality.yml:140,165`, `_eval-discipline.yml:74`, `test.yml:144`, `structured-output-baseline.yml:117`.\n- **PLW1510 is not test-only.** 318 of the 336 sit under `src` + `tests`; `make lint` covers all three trees.\n- **The ini mechanism is verified**, so only the marking sweep is open: the three keys are real `parser.addini` options in pytest-timeout 2.4.0, and on this venv they time out an unmarked 25 s test under `--strict-config` and pass the same test marked `timeout(60, func_only=True)`.\n- Marking precedes lowering: step 3 before step 4.\n\n## Scope\n`pyproject.toml` (ruff `select`; pytest ini keys); `Makefile` (`lint`); `.github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` (`:658`, `:673`); `tests/**` + `src/**` + `scripts/**` (the PLW1510 and selected-PT backlog); `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` (drift assertion); `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` (new); `docs/local-dev-env.md` (budget + override).\n\nReviewed, NOT changed: `test_ruff_ratchet.py`; the nine other workflow lanes; the two hygiene scripts.\n\n## Testing\n`tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py` holds both arms: a ~25 s test marked `timeout(60, func_only=True)` that passes, and a negative arm running `pytest` on a generated temp test in a subprocess with no `--timeout`, asserting a `Timeout` failure (a permanently red test cannot be committed). Pinning: `test_ruff_ratchet.py`, `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` and the two hygiene-lint tests stay green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nAll commands run from the worktree with `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\"` prepended.\n- [ ] The adopted codes are clean tree-wide. `ruff check --select PLW1510,PT001,PT006,PT007,PT008,PT012,PT013,PT017,PT021,PT022,PT028 src tests scripts` exits 0; today it exits 1 with 481 findings.\n- [ ] They are configured, not passed ad hoc. `python -c \"import tomllib; s=tomllib.load(open('pyproject.toml','rb'))['tool']['ruff']['lint']['select']; assert 'PLW1510' in s and 'PT001' in s\"` exits 0. Today: `AssertionError`.\n- [ ] `[tool.ruff.lint].ignore` is unchanged. `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ruff_ratchet.py -q` exits 0 (pinning).\n- [ ] The budget lives in the ini. `python -c \"import tomllib; p=tomllib.load(open('pyproject.toml','rb'))['tool']['pytest']['ini_options']; assert p['timeout']==20 and p['timeout_method']=='thread' and p['timeout_func_only'] is True\"` exits 0. Today: `KeyError: 'timeout'`.\n- [ ] Both budget arms hold under the ini alone. `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py -q` exits 0. Today pytest exits 4.\n- [ ] The two CI lanes carry the ini budget and keep their hang guard. `grep -c -- \"--timeout=20 --timeout-method=thread\" .github/workflows/_build-and-test.yml` prints `2` (today `0`), and `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py -q` exits 0 with the drift assertion in place.\n- [ ] `make lint` reaches both hygiene checks. `make -n lint | grep -c \"check_wall_clock_asserts.py\\|check_raw_git_writes.py\"` prints `2`; today `0`.\n- [ ] The default tier stays clean under the budget. `python -m pytest -m unit -n 4 --dist worksteal -q` reports no `Failed: Timeout` (pinning; measured clean 2026-08-21 at an explicit `--timeout=20`).\n- [ ] `make lint` exits 0."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787370989561836001,"uuid":"992800cb-34fc-46fe-8512-70f787f7a87e"}